    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d4">

                <pb facs="0013" n="5" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg5"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841.24/603½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to the Secretary of State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-05-16">May 16, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Cordell</hi>: I wish you would work out the
                    over-all arrangement between the United States and the British Government
                    relative to the consideration or considerations to be given us by the British in
                    return for the material provided under the Lend-Lease Act.<anchor n="11"
                        xml:id="d4-f1"/></p>
                <p>I should like to discuss it with you at an early opportunity because I think it
                    is important that we reach an agreement with the British at an early date.</p>
                <p>Although I presume the agreement will not provide primarily for a return to us of
                    cash, I think, nevertheless, you should consult with <pb facs="0014" n="6"
                        xml:id="pg6"/> Secretary Morgenthau in regard to the broad provisions of the
                    agreement.</p>
                <p>Very sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Franklin</hi> D. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Roosevelt</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d4-f1" n="11" xml:id="d4-f1-content">
                <p>Approved March 11, 1941; 55 Stat 31.</p>
